<% const s = it.spec;
const code = {
  'node-web': (id) => `src/features/${id}/index.ts`,
  'node-lib': (id) => `src/features/${id}.ts`,
  'python-service': (id) => `src/${it.names.snake}/features/${it.h.snake(id)}.py`,
  'wordpress': (id) => `src/Features/${it.h.pascal(id)}.php`,
}[s.stack.pack];
const adapter = {
  'node-web': (id) => `tests/adapters/${id}.ts`,
  'node-lib': (id) => `tests/adapters/${id}.ts`,
  'python-service': (id) => `tests/adapters/${it.h.snake(id)}.py`,
  'wordpress': (id) => `tests/Adapters/${it.h.pascal(id)}Adapter.php`,
}[s.stack.pack];
const features = it.features.filter((f) => !f.builtin);
-%>
# Plan 000: bootstrap <%= it.names.title %>

## Executor preamble

You are the first agent on this repository. The Incubator generated the canonical framework; your
job is the product. Implement the core features below in order, one step group per feature. For each
feature: implement its code, replace every `TODO(scaffold)` marker in its code and scenarios, turn its
four scenarios from `"status": "todo"` into real assertions, and keep `node scripts/check.mjs quick`
green after every step. Each feature has a ticket (`F-<id>`); move it through the lane's states and
stop at `READY_FOR_TEST`. Never improvise outside the files listed here: record a remediation item
instead.

<% if (features.length === 0) { -%>
No core features were recorded at discovery. Start by adding one with
`node scripts/scaffold.mjs feature <id> --summary "…"`.
<% } -%>
<% features.forEach((f, i) => { -%>
**Step <%= i + 1 %>:** <%= f.summary %> (`<%= f.id %>`, lane `<%= f.lane %>`).
- Target: <%= code(f.id) %>
- Target: tests/scenarios/<%= f.id %>/
- Target: <%= adapter(f.id) %>

<% }) -%>
## Touched files and markers

| Feature | Files | Markers |
|---|---|---|
| health (built in) | <%= code('health') %>, tests/scenarios/health/ | none (complete) |
<% for (const f of features) { -%>
| <%= f.id %> | <%= code(f.id) %>, tests/scenarios/<%= f.id %>/, <%= adapter(f.id) %> | `TODO(scaffold)` |
<% } -%>

## Acceptance commands

```sh
node scripts/check.mjs full
```

```text
exit 0 — completeness score ≥ <%= s.testing.completenessThreshold %>, coverage ≥ <%= s.testing.coverageThreshold %> %, every scenario active
```

## Drift and hallucination guardrails

| Trap | Why | Mechanical check |
|---|---|---|
| Editing `.incubator/lock.json` | The Incubator owns it; `sync` relies on it | agent profile denies it; `incubator sync` reports edits |
| Deleting or skipping a failing test | Hides regressions | `tests-collected` and the `scenarios` catalog-parity guard |
| Quarantining a test without an owner | Flakes become permanent | `quarantine` guard (owner + expiry required) |
| Adding code outside the registry | Features drift from their tests | `drift` guard (features ↔ scenarios ↔ adapters) |
| Absolute machine paths | Breaks every other machine | `abs-path` guard in `check` and pre-commit |
| Leaving `TODO(scaffold)` markers | Half-done scaffolding looks finished | `completeness` score |

